Fixtures from public archives (fixtures.toml has each file's URL and sha256, of the
original and of the cut):

- fixtures/emdb_map/EMD-3197.map: the map of the EMDB entry EMD-3197
  (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-3197), taken unchanged from mrcfile's test data
  (https://github.com/ccpem/mrcfile, tests/test_data/, at its tag v1.5.4), whose
  README says it was fetched from the EMDB.
- fixtures/emdb_tomogram/emd_66908.map: the header of the map of the EMDB entry
  EMD-66908, "Cryo-electron tomography of a synapse in cultured rat hippocampal
  neurons" (Lv ZY, Lu ZH, Liu S et al.), https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-66908.
- fixtures/epu_falcon/: the headers of two files of EMPIAR-12652, "TnsB strand
  transfer complex micrographs" (Tenjo-Castaño F, Sofos N, López-Méndez B et al.),
  https://www.ebi.ac.uk/empiar/EMPIAR-12652/.
- fixtures/epu_movie/: the header of one movie of EMPIAR-12018, "Cryo-EM of
  hMRS2-BRIL with EDTA" (He Z, Mount JW, Zhang J et al.),
  https://www.ebi.ac.uk/empiar/EMPIAR-12018/.
- fixtures/particle_stack/: the header of one particle stack of EMPIAR-11898,
  "Cryo-EM micrographs of engineered encapsulin P3P4" (Satler T, Jerala R et al.),
  https://www.ebi.ac.uk/empiar/EMPIAR-11898/.

Licence of these: CC0 1.0. EMPIAR: "All data in EMPIAR is freely and publicly
available to the global community under the CC0 license"
(https://www.ebi.ac.uk/empiar/faq, "Under what license is EMPIAR data available?",
read 2026-11-13). EMDB: the molecular and cellular structure archives at EMBL-EBI
(PDBe, EMDB and EMPIAR) "provide data available to all in accordance with the
Creative Commons Zero (CC0) designation"
(https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/about/public-data-access-statement, read 2026-11-13);
the wwPDB core archives likewise (https://www.wwpdb.org/about/usage-policies).
Please cite the entries' authors as a matter of good scientific practice.

- fixtures/fei1/fei-extended.mrc: the header of fei-extended.mrc of mrcfile's test
  data (https://github.com/ccpem/mrcfile, tests/test_data/, at its tag v1.5.4),
  whose README says: "fei-extended.mrc was contributed (along with permission for
  public distribution) by Kevin Savage at Diamond Light Source." mrcfile's
  repository is under the BSD 3-Clause licence, "Copyright (c) 2016, Science and
  Technology Facilities Council"; the file carries no licence of its own.

The rest of modama-formats-em, the other fixtures here included, is
MIT-licensed; see ../../../../LICENSE.
